In `store.js.es6` `_hydrateEmbedded`, the new plural-IDs branch (`/_(.+)_id(s?)$/` with `m[2]`) always does `delete obj[k];` after `map`, regardless of whether `_lookupSubType` resolves anything:

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(id => self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root));
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
delete obj[k];
```

Since `map` always returns an array, `hydrated || []` never falls back, and unresolved IDs become `undefined` entries while the original `xxx_ids` array is removed. This matches the finding’s described data-loss behavior. | In `store.js.es6` `_hydra

